sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Whether two adjacent cells in a filament (as in Nostoc and its allies) are separated by flat partitions, are hemispherical, or are each more than a hemisphere depends on the relative magnitudes of the tension at the outer cell surface and at the boundary between the cells.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Shape of paired cells depends on relative tensions at outer surface and partition";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter VII, “The Forms of Tissues, or Cell-Aggregates”; topic “Two-celled aggregates and partition walls”. Scope: pairs and chains of cells in filamentous lower algae and other two-celled aggregates"
}
